{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.PeriodicTableDemandConjecture","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.PeriodicTableDemandConjecture","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.magic_numbers_contain_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.magic_numbers_contain_two","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L101-L104","doc":"**SPECIAL CASE (provable).** The magic numbers list is non-empty\nand contains 2 (the lightest magic number). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.pb208_doubly_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.pb208_doubly_magic","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L96-L99","doc":"**CONDITIONAL.** Lead-208 is doubly magic (Z=82, N=126). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.o16_doubly_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.o16_doubly_magic","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L91-L94","doc":"**CONDITIONAL.** Oxygen-16 is doubly magic (Z=8, N=8). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.he4_doubly_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.he4_doubly_magic","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L83-L89","doc":"**CONDITIONAL.** Helium-4 is doubly magic (Z=2, N=2).\nIf the demand conjecture holds, then He-4 achieves demand\nclosure for both protons and neutrons — explaining its\nextraordinary stability (highest binding energy per nucleon). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.periodic_table_demand_conjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.periodic_table_demand_conjecture","kind":"instance","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L63-L74","doc":"**Canonical instance** — the conjecture proper. Each `sorry`\nis the unproved content of the corresponding claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.PeriodicTableDemand.drip_lines_from_demand_divergence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.PeriodicTableDemand.drip_lines_from_demand_divergence","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L61-L61","doc":"(iii) Drip lines ↔ demand divergence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.PeriodicTableDemand.noble_gas_shell_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.PeriodicTableDemand.noble_gas_shell_closure","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L59-L59","doc":"(ii) Noble gases ↔ atomic demand closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.PeriodicTableDemand.magic_numbers_from_demand_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.PeriodicTableDemand.magic_numbers_from_demand_closure","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L57-L57","doc":"(i) Magic numbers ↔ nuclear demand closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.PeriodicTableDemand.valley_of_stability_matches","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.PeriodicTableDemand.valley_of_stability_matches","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Main: ∀ A ≤ 238, the demand-minimizer is the observed valley. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.PeriodicTableDemand.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.PeriodicTableDemand.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.PeriodicTableDemand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.PeriodicTableDemand","kind":"class","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L49-L61","doc":"**Periodic-table demand conjecture** (axiomatised as a class\nper AGENTS.md §3b-cond). Main claim + three sub-claims.\nDownstream blocks may take `[PeriodicTableDemand]` as a class\nhypothesis. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:periodic-table-demand","label":"rem:periodic-table-demand","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.DripLinesFromDemandDivergenceHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.DripLinesFromDemandDivergenceHolds","kind":"opaque","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L44-L47","doc":"**Sub-claim (iii): drip lines from demand divergence**.\nThe proton (neutron) drip line is the locus where\n`|dem(N(Z, N))| → ∞` under adding a proton (neutron). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.NobleGasShellClosureHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.NobleGasShellClosureHolds","kind":"opaque","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L38-L42","doc":"**Sub-claim (ii): shell closure from electron demand**.\nThe noble gases (`Z = 2, 10, 18, 36, 54, 86`) are exactly\nthe values where the atom achieves\n`dem(A(Z, N*)) = ∅` for the most abundant stable isotope `N*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.MagicNumbersFromDemandClosureHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.MagicNumbersFromDemandClosureHolds","kind":"opaque","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L32-L36","doc":"**Sub-claim (i): magic numbers from demand closure**.\nThe nuclear magic numbers `{2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126}` are\nexactly the values of `Z` (or `N`) at which the nucleus\nachieves demand closure for at least one complementary value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.ValleyOfStabilityMatchesHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PeriodicTableDemand.ValleyOfStabilityMatchesHolds","kind":"opaque","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/periodic-table-demand-conjecture.lean#L27-L30","doc":"**Main claim**: for `A ≤ 238`, the demand-minimizing\n`(Z*, N*)` matches the experimentally observed valley of\nstability. ","signatureChunk":0}]}